# --- the court's input window opens around frame 594, so the pulses start there ---
#
# Measured, and the reason an earlier attempt at this repro did nothing at all.
# The court appears at frame 412 (camera 128 appears, the display records start
# populating at 421), but the game does not act on a direction until frame 594:
# pressing LEFT in 4-frame pulses leaves the camera at 128 until 594 and it then
# steps 128, 121, 115, 108, 102, 95, 89 ... Presses before 594 are silently
# dropped, which is also why tas/vectors/sdb_pan.input's LEFT at frame 500
# appears to do nothing and the motion only starts at 594.
#
# The pulses deliberately begin at 600 rather than 380: nothing is gained by
# pressing through the menus, and it makes the vector's intent obvious.
#
# Diagnostic only, not a test vector -- it exists to answer "when does the game
# start listening", and the answer is 594.
600 LEFT
